"{\"content\":\"Proof Obligations for sort_list (insertion sort)\\n================================================\\n\\nImplementation recap\\n--------------------\\n  def sort_list(items):\\n      result = list(items)                    # copy; OB1 concerns this\\n      for i in range(1, len(result)):         # outer loop, i = 1..n-1\\n          key = result[i]                     # key held OUT of the array\\n          j = i - 1\\n          while j >= 0 and result[j] > key:   # inner shift loop\\n              result[j + 1] = result[j]\\n              j -= 1\\n          result[j + 1] = key                 # key written back: Perm restored\\n      return result\\n\\nGoal (from formal_spec.txt):\\n  forall L. Sorted(sort_list(L)) and Perm(L, sort_list(L))\\n\\nNotation: a_0..a_{n-1} denote the elements of the input L; |L| = n.\\n\\\"sorted(s, e)\\\" means result[s..e] is non-decreasing.\\n\\n\\nLoop invariants\\n---------------\\nINV-OUT(i)  (before outer iteration i, 1 <= i <= n):\\n  (A) Perm(L, result)               -- multiset equality with the input\\n  (B) sorted(0, i-1)                -- prefix of length i is sorted\\n  (C) result[p] = a_p for all p >= i -- suffix untouched so far\\n\\nINV-IN(j)  (at the inner-loop guard, during outer iteration i,\\n            with key = a_i saved before any shift):\\n  (1) multiset(result) = multiset(L) - {key} + {result[j+1]}\\n        -- \\\"hole accounting\\\": key is held out; position j+1 is the\\n           hole, currently holding a duplicate of the shifted values\\n           (or key itself, if no shift has happened yet, j+1 = i)\\n  (2) result[0..j] = a_0..a_j  and  sorted(0, j)\\n  (3) result[j+2..i] = a_{j+1}..a_{i-1}  (the displaced prefix elements,\\n        still in their original sorted order), hence sorted(j+2, i)\\n        and every one of them > key\\n  (4) result[p] = a_p for all p >= i+1\\n\\n\\nObligations\\n-----------\\n\\nOB1  (Copy yields a permutation -- base permutation fact)\\n  After `result = list(items)`:\\n    Perm(L, result)  and  result[p] = a_p for all 0 <= p < n.\\n  Proof: elementwise copy; occ(x, copy(L)) = occ(x, L) for all x.\\n\\nOB2  (Inner invariant establishment)\\n  At the start of outer iteration i (1 <= i < n), from INV-OUT(i)\\n  and key = result[i] = a_i, j = i-1: INV-IN(i-1) holds.\\n  Checks: (1) hole is position i, holding key itself, so\\n  multiset(result) = multiset(L) - {key} + {key} = multiset(L);\\n  (2) prefix a_0..a_{i-1} sorted by INV-OUT(i).B; (3) range j+2..i\\n  is empty; (4) suffix by INV-OUT(i).C.\\n\\nOB3  (Inner invariant preservation -- shift step)\\n  If INV-IN(j) and the guard holds (j >= 0 and result[j] > key),\\n  then after `result[j+1] = result[j]; j -= 1`, INV-IN(j-1) holds.\\n  Proof sketch:\\n    - (1): the write replaces the hole content a_{j+1} (duplicated\\n      one slot up) by a_j; the new hole is at (j-1)+1 = j. Multiset\\n      changes by -{a_{j+1}} + {a_j} on both sides.\\n    - (2): positions 0..j-1 untouched, still a_0..a_{j-1}, sorted.\\n    - (3): new displaced region j+1..i = a_j followed by the old\\n      a_{j+1}..a_{i-1}; sorted since a_j <= a_{j+1} (original prefix\\n      sorted), and a_j > key by the guard.\\n    - (4): untouched.\\n  Termination (variant): j strictly decreases and is bounded below\\n  by -1 (guard requires j >= 0), so the inner loop terminates.\\n\\nOB4  (Inner exit -- key placement restores Perm and extends sortedness)\\n  If INV-IN(j) and the guard fails (j < 0 or result[j] <= key), then\\n  after `result[j+1] = key`, INV-OUT(i+1) holds:\\n    - (A) Perm: by (1), the multiset is multiset(L) - {key} +\\n      {result[j+1]}; the write replaces that hole value by key,\\n      restoring exactly multiset(L).\\n    - (B) sorted(0, i): head result[0..j] is sorted with all elements\\n      <= key (at exit result[j] <= key and the head is sorted; empty\\n      when j < 0); key sits at j+1; tail result[j+2..i] is sorted with\\n      all elements > key by (3). Edge case j+1 = i (no shift): the\\n      write is a no-op and sortedness of 0..i follows from the guard\\n      failure result[i-1] <= key alone.\\n    - (C) suffix: shifts and the write only touch positions <= i.\\n  This obligation discharges permutation preservation (with OB1, OB3)\\n  and the inductive step for sortedness.\\n\\nOB5  (Outer base case)\\n  INV-OUT(1) holds on loop entry: (A) by OB1; (B) sorted(0, 0) is\\n  trivial (single element); (C) by OB1. Degenerate inputs n <= 1\\n  never enter the loop, and OB1 + trivial sortedness give the\\n  postcondition directly.\\n\\nOB6  (Outer inductive step)\\n  For 1 <= i < n: INV-OUT(i) implies INV-OUT(i+1).\\n  Proof: OB2 establishes INV-IN, OB3 preserves it around the inner\\n  loop, OB4 closes the iteration. This is the main induction on i.\\n\\nOB7  (Postcondition at outer exit)\\n  At loop exit i = n: INV-OUT(n) gives sorted(0, n-1), i.e.\\n  Sorted(sort_list(L)), and Perm(L, result), i.e.\\n  Perm(L, sort_list(L)). Together with OB5 this proves the goal.\\n\\nOB8  (Termination)\\n  Outer variant: n - i strictly decreases each iteration and is\\n  bounded below by 0, so the outer loop terminates and sort_list\\n  returns (needed for OB7 to apply to the returned list).\\n\\n\\nSummary of the proof structure\\n------------------------------\\n  OB1  copy permutes                  -> Perm base\\n  OB2  inner invariants established   -> links outer/inner loops\\n  OB3  shift preserves invariants     -> inner inductive step (+ inner\\n                                          termination variant)\\n  OB4  exit restores Perm, extends sorted prefix\\n                                      -> permutation preservation and\\n                                         sortedness inductive step\\n  OB5  base case i = 1                -> sortedness base case\\n  OB6  outer inductive step           -> INV-OUT(i) for all i\\n  OB7  postcondition                  -> final theorem\\n  OB8  outer termination              -> totality of sort_list\\n\",\"path\":\"sorting_verification/obligations.txt\"}"